<title>USA: BellSouth Corp Q1 oper net increases.</title>
<headline>BellSouth Corp Q1 oper net increases.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF INCOME</p>
<p>		 (In Millions, Except Per Share Amounts)</p>
<p>				 (Unaudited)</p>
<p>					 1997	1996</p>
<p>Operating Revenues:</p>
<p>Network and related</p>
<p>services</p>
<p>  Local service		 $ 2,104   $ 1,930</p>
<p>  Interstate access		 917	 909</p>
<p>  Intrastate access		 218	 218</p>
<p>  Toll				  174	 207</p>
<p>  Wireless communications	 765	 625</p>
<p>Directory advertising</p>
<p>    and publishing		  361	 318</p>
<p>  Other services		    306	 334</p>
<p> Total Operating Revenues     4,845     4,541</p>
<p>Gain on Sale of Paging</p>
<p>   Business			   ---	 442</p>
<p>Other Income (Expense),</p>
<p>  net				   (7)	  36</p>
<p> Net income			   693	 970</p>
<p> Operating earnings per share  0.70	0.63</p>
<p>   Gain on Paging unit sale     ---     (0.35)</p>
<p> Net Earnings Per Share	  0.70	0.98</p>
<p>Weighted Average Common</p>
<p>  Shares Outstanding		992	 994</p>
<p>NOTE: One-time item in Q1 1996 reflects after-tax gain on sale of business. The pre-tax gain on the sale was $442 million and the after-tax gain was $344 million.</p>
<p>First Call consensus estimate for 1997 Q1 was $0.69 per share.</p>
<p>((--E. Auchard, New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1736))</p>
